HanaWorlds Workshop 0.1.0 component candidate.

HanaWorlds-owned source is MIT; see LICENSE. Workshop includes a byte-identical
runtime and one test-fixture subset of hanaworlds-contracts@0.3.4 from public
revision c00a489a6118fda68b80c7c1eee9a2aa90b6ddc0 (npm pack SHA256
9157fac5942b3604c8b145922c526f7ae6bdafc681ac8ac75feb2489bdddb8a2).
That source is MIT; its LICENSE, NOTICE, per-file hashes, import closure and
canonicalize Apache-2.0 license text are retained under vendor/contracts/.
The package installs canonicalize@5.1.0 separately from the public registry;
its Apache-2.0 license remains with that dependency. Workshop does not embed
the upstream canonicalize implementation.
The test-only `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-persistence-jsonl@0.2.0-rc.2` package
is MIT, sourced from the public npm registry / DeepSeek Harness repository,
and runs the isolated real Core Session JSONL recovery test; it is not bundled
into the Workshop runtime package.
The Core `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session@0.2.0-rc.2` runtime dependency and its
public `@deepseek-ai/cordis@4.0.4`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-scope@0.2.0-rc.2`,
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-invariants@0.2.0-rc.2`, and
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-storage-domain@0.2.0-rc.2` peers are separately installed
MIT packages. Workshop also uses `zod@4.6.5` for its durable projection schema.
Core DSH, its Session/Attachment services, and the PiAiAdapter are reused as
host services; their source and license are not copied into this package.
